          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Decibels and intensity",
              "marks": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p31-q1-intensity",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Sound intensity ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "I",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " is measured in watts per square metre (",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "\\mathrm{W/m^2}",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "). The reference intensity ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "I_0",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " represents the approximate threshold of human hearing and is taken to be ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "10^{-12}\\,\\mathrm{W/m^2}",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ". A close whisper has an intensity of about ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "100I_0",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": ".",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p31-q1-decibels",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Physicists and engineers often express sound level in decibels (dB). The decibel was named in honour of Alexander Graham Bell (1847–1922), known for his work on the telephone. The sound level ",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "L",
              "display": false
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": " in decibels is given by",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p31-q1-formula",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "center",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "latex": "L=10\\log_{10}\\!\\left(\\frac{I}{I_0}\\right).",
              "display": true
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p31-q1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Draw a graph of sound level $L$ against intensity $I$. Leave room to mark the points from parts (b) and (c) on the same graph.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "sharedSolutionDiagramId": "p31-q1-solution-graph",
        "answer": {
          "short": "Draw an increasing logarithmic curve for $I>0$, with $I$ on the horizontal axis and $L$ on the vertical axis. It crosses $L=0$ at $I=10^{-12}\\,\\mathrm{W/m^2}$.",
          "worked": "Use powers of ten to choose points. For example, at $I=10^{-8}\\,\\mathrm{W/m^2}$,\n$$\\begin{align*}L&=10\\log_{10}\\!\\left(\\frac{10^{-8}}{10^{-12}}\\right)\\\\L&=10\\log_{10}(10^4)\\\\L&=40\\,\\mathrm{dB}.\\end{align*}$$\nIntensities of $10^{-9}$, $10^{-7}$, $10^{-6}$ and $10^{-5}\\,\\mathrm{W/m^2}$ give $30$, $50$, $60$ and $70\\,\\mathrm{dB}$ respectively. Plot these points and draw a smooth increasing curve that flattens as $I$ increases. The full curve crosses $L=0$ when $I=I_0$ and has vertical asymptote $I=0$. The figure shows the portion used to mark the two examples in part (d).",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 44
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Normal conversation has an intensity of about $10^{-6}\\,\\mathrm{W/m^2}$. Calculate the corresponding sound level in decibels.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "About $60\\,\\mathrm{dB}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}L&=10\\log_{10}\\!\\left(\\frac{10^{-6}}{10^{-12}}\\right)\\\\L&=10\\log_{10}(10^6)\\\\L&=60\\,\\mathrm{dB}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 20
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "A busy street has a sound level of about $70\\,\\mathrm{dB}$. Calculate the corresponding intensity.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "About $10^{-5}\\,\\mathrm{W/m^2}$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}70&=10\\log_{10}\\!\\left(\\frac{I}{I_0}\\right)\\\\\\log_{10}\\!\\left(\\frac{I}{I_0}\\right)&=7\\\\\\frac{I}{I_0}&=10^7\\\\I&=10^7\\times 10^{-12}\\,\\mathrm{W/m^2}\\\\I&=10^{-5}\\,\\mathrm{W/m^2}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 26
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q1-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Plot and label the points for normal conversation and a busy street on your graph from part (a).",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "sharedSolutionDiagramId": "p31-q1-solution-graph",
        "answer": {
          "short": "Normal conversation $(10^{-6},60)$ and busy street $(10^{-5},70)$, with coordinates in $(\\mathrm{W/m^2},\\mathrm{dB})$.",
          "worked": "Use the intensities as horizontal coordinates and the sound levels as vertical coordinates. On the axis scaled in units of $10^{-6}\\,\\mathrm{W/m^2}$, mark normal conversation at $(1,60)$ and the busy street at $(10,70)$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p31-q1-solution-graph",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"curveBlue\",\"hex\":\"268CFF\",\"reason\":\"logarithmic model curve\"}],\"reference\":\"PDF page 31, p31-q1-solution-graph\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.72cm,y=0.10cm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\definecolor{curveBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}\n\\draw[black,line width=0.5pt,->] (0,0) -- (12.8,0);\n\\draw[black,line width=0.5pt,->] (0,0) -- (0,45) node[above] {$L\\ (\\mathrm{dB})$};\n\\foreach \\u in {0,1,2,4,6,8,10,12}{\n  \\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (\\u,0) -- ++(0,-1.2);\n  \\node[below] at (\\u,-1.2) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}$\\u$\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};\n}\n\\foreach \\v/\\n in {0/30,10/40,20/50,30/60,40/70}{\n  \\draw[black,line width=0.4pt] (0,\\v) -- ++(-0.16,0);\n  \\node[left] at (-0.16,\\v) {\\special{dvisvgm:raw <g data-graph-text=\"tick\">}$\\n$\\special{dvisvgm:raw </g>}};\n}\n\\node[below] at (6.4,-7) {$I\\ (10^{-6}\\,\\mathrm{W/m^2})$};\n\\draw[curveBlue,line width=0.8pt,->,domain=30:70.79,samples=90,variable=\\t] plot ({pow(10,(\\t-60)/10)},{\\t-30});\n\\fill[black] (1,30) circle[radius=1.45pt] node[below right] {Normal conversation};\n\\fill[black] (10,40) circle[radius=1.45pt] node[above left] {Busy street};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
              "src": null,
              "widthMm": 108,
              "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
              "overlayOf": null,
              "transparent": false,
              "axes": null,
              "spec": {
                "sourcePage": 31,
                "sourceRegion": "Question 1(a) and (d)",
                "description": "Shared solution graph for parts (a) and (d). The linear intensity axis is scaled in millionths of a watt per square metre. The view starts at 30 dB to show both examples clearly.",
                "mathematics": "For horizontal coordinate u = I/(10^-6 W/m²), L = 60 + 10 log10(u). The plotted parametrisation is u = 10^(L/10 - 6). The labelled points are (1,60) and (10,70) in the displayed units. The full curve has asymptote I = 0 and crosses L = 0 at I = 10^-12 W/m².",
                "answerVisibility": "solution only"
              },
              "derived": false,
              "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
            }
          ]
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "p31-q1-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "Explain why using only intensity to measure sound may be impractical.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Sound intensities span many powers of ten. The decibel scale compresses that range.",
          "worked": "Raw intensities can be very small and can differ by large factors. On the logarithmic scale, every tenfold increase in intensity adds $10\\,\\mathrm{dB}$. For example, the busy street has ten times the intensity of normal conversation, while its sound level is only $10\\,\\mathrm{dB}$ higher.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      }
    ]
  },
